## Решение

Replace the manifest-only continuation loop with the sequence in [development sequence](../findings/D2-development-sequence.md). Missing receipts are outputs of named producer tasks, not an open-ended questionnaire for the owner. Preserve historical terminal P1/P2/P3/P6.1 and all their actual proof scopes. Refine only unfinished items: original P4.3 is decomposed into sequential P4.3 pair store, P4.4 expiry, P4.5 credentials, P4.6 inbox and P4.7 final composition; add external qualification/adoption phase P7. No terminal item is renumbered.

Two independent proof contours:

- Local library engineering and isolated acceptance: P4/P5; local same-source packet P6.2. Local source/fixture proofs never qualify effective DI/AP.
- Owning API/storage/profile acceptance, central/cloud deployment, executed membership acceptance and distribution: P7.1–P7.5. Every effective DI/AP remains UNFILLED until all its mandatory subconditions are evidenced.

P4 order: P4.1 → P4.2 → P4.3 → P4.4 → P4.5 → P4.6 → P4.7. P5.1 becomes dependency-ready after P4.2 and may proceed independently of session integration. P6.2 consumes local package receipts only and may list external gaps without claiming membership or consumer release. P7.3 is the named accepted-facade/storage/profile code adoption producer after P7.1/P7.2 accepted target evidence; actual deployment precedes P7.4 AP. P7 preparation can proceed independently; its admission/qualification consumes actual owning evidence only.

Routine decisions: choose the smallest reversible implementation satisfying D6; deterministic per-package fixtures; explicit deny when deployment/profile adapter is absent; preserve existing published surface; no new mandatory auth dependency; no tenant central writer; no production schema inferred from disposable fixtures. Implementer prepares exact API/BC/storage/CHANGELOG decision carriers itself before a protected mutation. A single concrete owning decision can cover a bounded local tranche; central deployment is not a prerequisite for isolated library proof.

## Authority retained

**D2 NOT released for implementation.** This record does not supersede D6 or mint a public API/storage/release grant. A future code invocation must have explicit bounded local implementation authority; any changed existing public API additionally requires the exact contract-owner/major decision. Neither routine autonomy nor a synthetic profile grants central/cloud binding, production schema, private install, commit or external writes. Preparation, draft specifications and read-only preflight continue without asking the owner for a manifest.

## Почему

The old continuation required deployment and full membership acceptance before engineering the library/test seams that produce part of those proofs. P4.7 also excluded new schema while its D6 logical fences require an approved physical mapping, and combined storage, clock, credential final write, scheduler and retry into one item. Separating producers eliminates circular readiness without weakening acceptance.

## Consequences

Questions are limited to a real product outcome or finite ungranted authority, with a concrete prepared choice. Missing central source does not trigger another inventory/framework refresh. Each stopped external task records its exact missing receipt/owner/action and the scheduler continues other ready local tasks. No new owning receipt, effective deployment or executed AP is claimed by this plan revision.
